{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Breakpoint.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Breakpoint.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"breakpoint breakpoint","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Breakpoint.md","fileName":"Breakpoint.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Breakpoint","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 20:37\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Application Debugging]] [[C Sharp Functions Diagnostics and Testing]] [[Visual Studio Development Workflow]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Application Debugging","C Sharp Functions Diagnostics and Testing","Visual Studio Development Workflow","Debugger","hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf","aspnetcore3andangular9_3ed.pdf","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Breakpoint.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Breakpoint.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"breakpoint breakpoint","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Breakpoint.md","fileName":"Breakpoint.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Breakpoint","heading":"Breakpoint","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A breakpoint marks a source location where a [[Debugger]] should pause program execution. While paused, a developer can inspect variables, evaluate expressions, review the call stack, and step through subsequent operations.\n\nA breakpoint inside a controller can expose server request state, while one in an Angular component can expose form or subscription state. Conditions can narrow the pause to a relevant case.\n\nA Visual Studio breakpoint can also carry a label, a Boolean condition, and an action. The Breakpoints window makes those stops manageable across a solution, while step-into, step-over, and step-out commands continue execution at different call depths.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Application Debugging